positive:
Of verdure, field from field, as man from man;
The skies themselves looked low and positive,
As almost you could touch them with a hand,

posture:
And crash it out with clangour. I was weak;
I struggled for the posture of my soul
In upright consciousness of place and time,

possums:
Tells de folks we 's on de track.
Coons is a-ramblin' an' 'possums is out;
Look at dat dog; you could set on his tail!

posies:
Leave me to my lonely pillow.
Go, and take your silly posies;
Who has vowed to wear the willow

possum's:
Cain't you stan' to hyeah about it? S'pose you'd been an' seed it all;
Seed dem gread big sweet pertaters, layin' by de possum's side,
Seed dat coon in all his gravy, reckon den you 'd up and died!

possest:
HAIL, happy saint, on thine immortal throne,
Possest of glory, life, and bliss unknown;
We hear no more the music of thy tongue,

postures:
And sighed my soul out. The most utter wretch
Will choose his postures when he comes to die,
However in the presence of a queen;

